Lossless Library Sync (`crates/spotisync` and Spotifast sync integration)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------

The `crates/spotisync` workspace crate and its integration in Spotifast
(`src/sync_bridge.rs`, `src/local_player.rs`, and related settings, credential,
and UI modules) are original, clean-room MIT-licensed implementations written
from observed public provider HTTP API behaviour.

No LGPL-3.0 or GPL-licensed code was copied from SpotiFLAC, streamrip, or any
other third-party downloader. Both projects are acknowledged solely as
conceptual inspiration for lossless playlist archiving workflows.

Spotify Premium remains required for Spotify playback. Nothing in Spotifast or
`spotisync` circumvents DRM, extracts keys from Spotify, or redistributes
Spotify binaries.

Key crates.io dependencies introduced for `crates/spotisync`
------------------------------------------------------------

All crates in `crates/spotisync/Cargo.toml` come from crates.io under
permissive licenses compatible with MIT:

- `rusqlite` (0.32, MIT License) with the `bundled` feature via
  `libsqlite3-sys` (MIT License), which statically compiles SQLite
  (Public Domain).
- `lofty` (0.25, MIT OR Apache-2.0 License) for pure-Rust FLAC stream property
  inspection, Vorbis comment tagging, and embedded cover picture blocks.
- `async-trait` (0.1, MIT OR Apache-2.0 License) for async trait objects on
  `Provider` and `PlaylistSource`.
- `bytes` (1, MIT License) for zero-copy HTTP audio payload buffers.
- `tempfile` (3, MIT OR Apache-2.0 License, dev-dependency) for isolated test
  directories.

`crates/spotisync` also reuses crates already present in the Spotifast
workspace (`http`, `log`, `md-5`, `rand`, `reqwest`, `serde`, `serde_json`,
`thiserror`, and `tokio`), all under MIT or dual MIT / Apache-2.0 licenses.
Track title and artist fuzzy matching (Jaro-Winkler and normalized Levenshtein)
is implemented directly inside `crates/spotisync/src/matching.rs` with no
additional string-similarity crate.
